WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.040 --> 00:02.960
[The D Dorm]

3
00:02.980 --> 00:03.790
Ugh...

4
00:04.380 --> 00:06.190
We still have eight rooms left unchecked.

5
00:06.940 --> 00:08.360
I think Grandma Gaysorn's relative

6
00:08.360 --> 00:09.790
must be in one of these rooms.

7
00:09.790 --> 00:10.720
Mm, here...

8
00:10.720 --> 00:11.620
Take this.

9
00:11.760 --> 00:12.190
Here...

10
00:13.100 --> 00:13.810
- Hey... - Will you show up?

11
00:14.780 --> 00:15.450
Whoa, whoa!

12
00:15.570 --> 00:16.320
Calm down, Dobby.

13
00:16.320 --> 00:17.290
What the hell are you doing?

14
00:17.290 --> 00:18.420
I'm torturing Grandpa.

15
00:18.420 --> 00:20.240
He hasn't shown up for a few days.

16
00:20.240 --> 00:21.790
I lit the incense, but got no answer.

17
00:21.920 --> 00:22.990
Giving alms to the monk didn't work.

18
00:23.120 --> 00:24.420
So I'm trying to...

19
00:24.560 --> 00:25.580
provoke him,

20
00:25.580 --> 00:26.450
in case he shows up.

21
00:27.900 --> 00:28.770
Stop it.

22
00:29.210 --> 00:30.440
He must have fainted by now.

23
00:31.040 --> 00:32.590
Or did he reincarnate?

24
00:32.810 --> 00:34.250
Hey, are you crazy?

25
00:34.250 --> 00:35.580
He wouldn't reincarnate

26
00:35.580 --> 00:37.140
since he hasn't met Grandma Gaysorn yet.

27
00:37.390 --> 00:38.410
Whoa, be more gentle with that...

28
00:38.590 --> 00:39.790
If that doesn't work,

29
00:40.320 --> 00:41.120
I have another idea.

30
00:41.250 --> 00:43.390
You have an important keepsake, right?

31
00:43.390 --> 00:44.740
Fine, then.

32
00:44.940 --> 00:45.460
Move.

33
00:45.620 --> 00:46.400
Mm.

34
00:49.220 --> 00:50.140
Look!

35
00:52.280 --> 00:53.730
Hey, go back to where you were.

36
00:53.730 --> 00:54.650
- Ugh, I have to be here, too... - Yeah.

37
00:54.650 --> 00:55.390
Stand there.

38
00:55.390 --> 00:56.170
Hey!

39
00:56.330 --> 00:57.790
If you still don't show up,

40
00:58.500 --> 01:00.620
I'm going to burn this powder bottle.

41
01:00.620 --> 01:02.340
It's something you cherish, isn't it?

42
01:03.180 --> 01:04.440
Will you come out or not?

43
01:04.849 --> 01:06.190
Will you come out?

44
01:06.400 --> 01:07.080
Hey!

45
01:07.580 --> 01:08.450
- You! - Ow!

46
01:08.450 --> 01:09.789
What the hell are you doing?!

47
01:09.970 --> 01:11.810
This is Gramps' keepsake

48
01:11.810 --> 01:13.100
for when he misses his grandson.

49
01:14.800 --> 01:15.789
[Little Cloud]

50
01:15.980 --> 01:16.690
Wait...

51
01:16.690 --> 01:17.620
Gramps' grandson...

52
01:18.190 --> 01:19.280
That's you, isn't it?

53
01:20.960 --> 01:22.700
Then the naked baby here...

54
01:22.700 --> 01:23.580
is you?

55
01:24.190 --> 01:25.180
Do we look familiar?

56
01:25.970 --> 01:26.880
Yeah, you do.

57
01:28.800 --> 01:30.000
You're in trouble, Dobby.

58
01:30.000 --> 01:30.760
Now

59
01:30.760 --> 01:31.960
Ms. Danis knows

60
01:31.960 --> 01:33.680
that you're on the bottle.

61
01:33.680 --> 01:34.620
And you have the nickname

62
01:34.759 --> 01:36.770
Little Eggy.

63
01:36.770 --> 01:37.560
Hey...

64
01:37.560 --> 01:38.930
- Why did you say that? - Ow.

65
01:39.560 --> 01:40.990
- Little Eggy. - Hey.

66
01:40.990 --> 01:41.600
Little...

67
01:42.110 --> 01:43.390
Now everyone knows.

68
01:43.840 --> 01:44.460
Hey,

69
01:44.700 --> 01:45.620
can I ask you something?

70
01:45.620 --> 01:46.120
What?

71
01:46.120 --> 01:47.650
Don't tell anyone about this.

72
01:47.650 --> 01:48.420
It's embarrassing.

73
01:48.720 --> 01:49.840
Don't worry,

74
01:50.590 --> 01:51.789
everybody already knows.

75
01:51.789 --> 01:52.460
Huh?!

76
01:52.800 --> 01:53.729
Well, Gramps

77
01:53.729 --> 01:55.860
went around and bragged to the entire dorm

78
01:55.860 --> 01:57.530
that the boy on the bottle of powder

79
01:57.530 --> 01:58.650
is his grandson.

80
01:58.990 --> 01:59.690
See?

81
02:01.850 --> 02:02.440
Ugh...

82
02:02.590 --> 02:03.790
So, why are you here today?

83
02:03.790 --> 02:05.620
I brought the documents for you to sign.

84
02:05.620 --> 02:07.780
And I'm going to leave today.

85
02:08.009 --> 02:09.009
Are you going to quit?

86
02:09.789 --> 02:12.010
I'm asking for personal leave!

87
02:12.460 --> 02:13.640
My mother is sick today.

88
02:14.200 --> 02:14.860
Hey, wait...

89
02:15.320 --> 02:16.260
You're an orphan, aren't you?

90
02:17.460 --> 02:19.850
The kids at my orphanage

91
02:20.130 --> 02:20.860
call the director

92
02:20.860 --> 02:22.320
"Mother."

93
02:23.420 --> 02:23.970
I see.

94
02:24.410 --> 02:25.210
Okay, alright...

95
02:25.390 --> 02:25.960
You'd...

96
02:26.300 --> 02:27.250
better go see her soon.

97
02:27.650 --> 02:28.610
Sign the documents

98
02:28.610 --> 02:30.190
by this evening.

99
02:30.930 --> 02:32.210
Little Eggy.

100
02:33.120 --> 02:34.170
Little Eggy...

101
02:35.180 --> 02:37.390
I'll tell Auntie Duang about this.

102
02:38.590 --> 02:39.790
Little Eggy.

103
02:39.820 --> 02:40.760
Little... You little...

104
02:40.780 --> 02:42.210
Dax, this is your fault.

105
02:42.400 --> 02:43.620
- It's all because of you. - Stop, stop...

106
02:43.620 --> 02:44.590
Hey, wait, one sec.

107
02:46.460 --> 02:46.990
Oh?

108
02:47.920 --> 02:48.730
- Dax. - Hm?

109
02:49.579 --> 02:50.940
Mr. Sompong texted me.

110
02:51.320 --> 02:52.210
Little Eggy?

111
02:52.210 --> 02:52.990
No,

112
02:52.990 --> 02:53.810
take this seriously.

113
02:54.620 --> 02:56.130
"Can we meet to discuss

114
02:56.130 --> 02:57.790
what we're going to do about selling the dorm?"

115
02:57.790 --> 02:59.410
I've already put off the meeting about

116
02:59.410 --> 03:00.420
selling the dorm a few times.

117
03:03.240 --> 03:03.790
Uh...

118
03:04.240 --> 03:04.990
- Hey. - Hm?

119
03:04.990 --> 03:05.890
Don't worry, Dobby.

120
03:06.330 --> 03:07.170
You've got me.

121
03:07.390 --> 03:09.060
Every solution has a problem.

122
03:09.260 --> 03:10.440
Isn't it "Every problem has a solution"?

123
03:12.050 --> 03:12.940
Yeah, that one.

124
03:12.940 --> 03:13.780
I don't want you to feel stressed.

125
03:14.050 --> 03:14.810
Little Eggy...

126
03:16.640 --> 03:18.190
If you say that again, I'll slap you.

127
03:18.700 --> 03:19.650
Do it on the left side.

128
03:23.180 --> 03:30.990
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

129
03:32.990 --> 03:39.910
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

130
03:39.930 --> 03:45.829
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

131
03:47.340 --> 03:53.660
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

132
03:54.430 --> 03:58.930
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

133
03:58.930 --> 04:02.580
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

134
04:02.580 --> 04:06.170
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

135
04:06.170 --> 04:09.090
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

136
04:09.740 --> 04:12.220
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

137
04:12.220 --> 04:19.120
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

138
04:19.120 --> 04:26.320
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

139
04:26.320 --> 04:33.520
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

140
04:33.520 --> 04:40.720
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫

141
04:40.720 --> 04:44.590
[The D Dorm]

142
04:50.260 --> 04:51.100
Mr. Sompong,

143
04:51.650 --> 04:53.760
I'm definitely going to sell the dorm,

144
04:53.960 --> 04:55.620
but I'm having some trouble with the tenants.

145
04:55.760 --> 04:56.420
Well...

146
04:56.900 --> 04:57.790
most of them

147
04:57.980 --> 04:59.420
have year-long leases.

148
05:00.190 --> 05:01.060
If they don't leave,

149
05:01.540 --> 05:02.590
there's nothing I can do.

150
05:02.880 --> 05:04.760
Didn't you tell me

151
05:04.990 --> 05:06.440
you'd negotiate with them?

152
05:06.650 --> 05:08.590
I can't wait for a whole year.

153
05:09.560 --> 05:10.440
How about this?

154
05:10.720 --> 05:13.210
I'll go convince everyone to move out.

155
05:13.210 --> 05:14.180
I'm not leaving!

156
05:18.610 --> 05:19.730
How else will I make a living?

157
05:20.450 --> 05:20.960
Uh...

158
05:21.160 --> 05:22.180
who are you?

159
05:22.800 --> 05:23.440
That's

160
05:23.970 --> 05:25.600
one of the tenants in my dorm.

161
05:25.860 --> 05:26.880
He probably followed me.

162
05:27.050 --> 05:28.990
It's just a small square room,

163
05:33.360 --> 05:34.880
but it's still precious to me!

164
05:35.930 --> 05:37.170
My memories

165
05:37.170 --> 05:38.590
linger in every corner of the room!

166
05:39.170 --> 05:40.990
Ugh, I can't tell where this is going.

167
05:40.990 --> 05:41.730
Uh...

168
05:41.860 --> 05:42.920
can you elaborate?

169
05:42.920 --> 05:43.850
Grandpa and Grandma

170
05:44.130 --> 05:45.260
are pounding on the balcony!

171
05:46.659 --> 05:47.290
Pound what?

172
05:47.420 --> 05:48.190
Betel quid.

173
05:48.190 --> 05:48.740
Phew...

174
05:49.900 --> 05:50.960
Grandfather and Grandmother

175
05:50.960 --> 05:52.080
are busy in the corner of the room!

176
05:53.170 --> 05:53.920
Busy doing what?

177
05:54.330 --> 05:55.080
Plucking gray hairs.

178
05:56.220 --> 05:57.300
Uncle and Auntie

179
05:57.300 --> 05:58.730
like it filthy!

180
05:58.730 --> 05:59.290
What?

181
05:59.560 --> 06:00.190
Why?

182
06:00.320 --> 06:00.940
They own a laundromat.

183
06:00.970 --> 06:01.920
Oh... Laundromat.

184
06:03.340 --> 06:03.690
Unkie...

185
06:04.060 --> 06:04.770
Aunty...

186
06:04.770 --> 06:06.040
Dad, and Mom...

187
06:06.190 --> 06:06.960
are going at it on the bed!

188
06:07.680 --> 06:08.590
Go where?

189
06:08.590 --> 06:09.300
Go to sleep!

190
06:10.400 --> 06:11.420
Poor thing.

191
06:12.420 --> 06:13.390
Wait, wait, wait.

192
06:13.390 --> 06:15.790
Why are there so many people in such a small room?

193
06:16.240 --> 06:17.100
My room may be small,

194
06:17.460 --> 06:18.740
but my thing is huge.

195
06:19.160 --> 06:19.920
What's huge?

196
06:19.920 --> 06:20.740
The memories I made.

197
06:22.060 --> 06:22.800
See?

198
06:22.990 --> 06:24.190
His memories are huge to him.

199
06:24.500 --> 06:25.390
I don't care.

200
06:25.890 --> 06:26.590
I'm not leaving,

201
06:26.590 --> 06:28.250
no matter what!

202
06:29.600 --> 06:30.570
You... What is this?

203
06:30.570 --> 06:31.240
Mr. Sompong,

204
06:31.240 --> 06:32.200
let me handle this.

205
06:32.200 --> 06:32.820
Hey...

206
06:33.000 --> 06:33.790
- Mr. Dax! - I'm not leaving!

207
06:33.940 --> 06:34.840
Mr. Dax, calm down.

208
06:34.840 --> 06:35.490
Calm down.

209
06:35.490 --> 06:36.190
- Leave for now. - No.

210
06:36.300 --> 06:37.180
I'll talk to him.

211
06:37.180 --> 06:38.090
Mr. Dax, please leave.

212
06:38.280 --> 06:38.720
I'm not leaving.

213
06:38.720 --> 06:39.420
Mr. Dax, calm down.

214
06:39.420 --> 06:40.090
I'm not leaving.

215
06:40.090 --> 06:40.760
Mr. Dax!

216
06:40.760 --> 06:42.570
Can you please calm down for a bit?

217
06:42.570 --> 06:43.210
No,

218
06:43.210 --> 06:43.850
I'm not leaving.

219
06:45.960 --> 06:46.990
Mr. Sompong,

220
06:47.800 --> 06:48.900
that was just one person.

221
06:49.090 --> 06:50.060
At the dorm...

222
06:50.060 --> 06:51.610
there are problem tenants in more than ten rooms.

223
06:51.610 --> 06:52.300
Ten rooms?!

224
06:52.300 --> 06:52.990
That's right.

225
06:53.180 --> 06:54.490
Whoa, what should we do, then?

226
06:54.490 --> 06:56.960
My project can't be delayed any longer.

227
07:00.190 --> 07:01.090
Three months!

228
07:01.810 --> 07:03.140
Give me three months.

229
07:03.930 --> 07:06.720
I'll definitely get this dorm ready for sale, Mr. Sompong.

230
07:08.130 --> 07:08.590
Alright.

231
07:09.480 --> 07:11.820
But you have to sign a contract with me this time.

232
07:12.190 --> 07:12.920
Of course.

233
07:14.240 --> 07:17.130
Oh, the Feng Shui Master I told you about...

234
07:17.130 --> 07:18.190
- They will... - Oh.

235
07:18.190 --> 07:19.100
Mr. Sompong,

236
07:19.250 --> 07:20.320
I don't think that's necessary.

237
07:20.460 --> 07:22.440
You can bring him here after three months.

238
07:22.440 --> 07:24.450
Oh, I wanted to tell you that I won't be bringing him here anymore.

239
07:24.450 --> 07:25.700
Oh, you won't?

240
07:25.700 --> 07:28.020
My boss will hire a shaman to handle this instead.

241
07:28.020 --> 07:28.800
Huh?!

242
07:29.240 --> 07:29.970
A shaman?!

243
07:29.970 --> 07:30.440
Mm.

244
07:31.350 --> 07:32.250
When will he arrive?

245
07:32.590 --> 07:34.460
I heard he arrived a few days ago.

246
07:34.460 --> 07:35.540
A few days ago?!

247
07:35.540 --> 07:37.280
My boss picked him himself.

248
07:37.280 --> 07:38.590
He's very talented.

249
07:38.780 --> 07:41.540
He's sealed ghosts in pots countless times.

250
07:41.710 --> 07:43.100
Your grandpa already passed, right?

251
07:43.120 --> 07:43.390
Yes.

252
07:43.520 --> 07:44.970
This time, your grandpa will be...

253
07:44.990 --> 07:45.840
dead dead.

254
07:46.990 --> 07:48.190
Dead dead?

255
07:50.590 --> 07:51.620
Dead dead.

256
07:53.400 --> 07:55.620
Was the reason Grandpa vanished...

257
07:55.620 --> 07:57.010
because he was sealed in a pot...

258
07:57.010 --> 07:59.640
and he's now dead dead?!

259
08:00.450 --> 08:01.220
Grandpa.

260
08:01.220 --> 08:02.400
Gramps, are you there?

261
08:02.590 --> 08:03.280
Grandpa.

262
08:03.280 --> 08:04.990
Gramps, come out and see Dobby.

263
08:05.210 --> 08:05.970
Grandpa!

264
08:06.300 --> 08:07.810
- Gramps! - Grandpa!

265
08:10.100 --> 08:10.990
Grandpa.

266
08:12.190 --> 08:12.680
What?

267
08:12.800 --> 08:14.000
Grandpa, come out already.

268
08:14.800 --> 08:15.790
Gramps.

269
08:16.120 --> 08:16.990
Gramps.

270
08:19.840 --> 08:20.590
Grandpa!

271
08:22.380 --> 08:23.200
Grandpa!

272
08:23.440 --> 08:24.600
Hey, where did he go?

273
08:26.780 --> 08:28.240
- Gramps! - Grandpa!

274
08:28.240 --> 08:28.990
Gramps?

275
08:28.990 --> 08:30.000
- Grandpa! - Gramps...

276
08:30.000 --> 08:31.050
Gramps.

277
08:31.050 --> 08:31.850
Gramps?

278
08:32.620 --> 08:33.250
Hey...

279
08:33.500 --> 08:35.280
If he really was captured by the shaman,

280
08:35.280 --> 08:36.419
wouldn't that be great?

281
08:36.559 --> 08:38.080
That way, you could sell this dorm.

282
08:40.860 --> 08:41.919
How could I do that?

283
08:42.059 --> 08:43.620
I don't wanna break the promise I made to him.

284
08:43.620 --> 08:44.100
Oh?

285
08:44.100 --> 08:45.790
I want to keep my word.

286
08:45.790 --> 08:46.560
Hey,

287
08:46.560 --> 08:47.440
that's suspicious.

288
08:47.440 --> 08:48.190
Does this mean...

289
08:48.330 --> 08:51.190
you're starting to love him?

290
08:51.190 --> 08:52.530
Little Eggy.

291
08:52.740 --> 08:54.190
Little Eggy.

292
08:54.190 --> 08:55.390
Little Eggy...

293
08:58.360 --> 08:58.990
- Huh? - What?

294
08:59.800 --> 09:00.190
Huh?

295
09:00.780 --> 09:01.700
What is this piece of cloth?

296
09:04.320 --> 09:05.420
Give it back.

297
09:29.540 --> 09:32.590
[Don, occupation: Master]

298
09:33.360 --> 09:35.240
It's as if he just came out of 'Khemjira The Series.'

299
09:35.520 --> 09:38.210
♫Should any magic♫

300
09:38.210 --> 09:38.590
Hey!

301
09:40.120 --> 09:41.280
You're delusional, aren't you?

302
09:42.560 --> 09:43.720
How I dress is up to me,

303
09:44.300 --> 09:45.420
and it shouldn't be

304
09:45.680 --> 09:47.090
any of your business.

305
09:47.330 --> 09:49.880
- Ooh, - Ooh,

306
09:49.880 --> 09:52.000
- that hurts. - that hurts.

307
09:54.140 --> 09:54.710
Hey,

308
09:55.020 --> 09:56.250
do you live here?

309
09:58.770 --> 10:00.410
What's that pot

310
10:00.960 --> 10:01.760
in your hand?

311
10:03.750 --> 10:05.320
And this pot

312
10:05.560 --> 10:07.020
is none of your concern.

313
10:07.260 --> 10:09.490
- Ooh, - Ooh.

314
10:09.510 --> 10:10.880
not our business, huh...

315
10:14.860 --> 10:15.790
He's a feisty one.

316
10:15.790 --> 10:16.840
Yeah...

317
10:18.890 --> 10:20.290
Did you see that hand in his pot?

318
10:20.290 --> 10:20.980
Hey!

319
10:21.100 --> 10:21.790
Pot in his hand.

320
10:22.490 --> 10:23.410
That pot in his hand?

321
10:23.560 --> 10:24.190
Yeah.

322
10:25.090 --> 10:26.010
He might be...

323
10:26.220 --> 10:27.490
the shaman Mr. Sompong's boss

324
10:27.490 --> 10:29.220
sent to exorcise my grandpa.

325
10:30.060 --> 10:30.970
You might be right...

326
10:32.800 --> 10:33.790
Whoa,

327
10:34.280 --> 10:35.920
you're about to kiss the screen.

328
10:36.490 --> 10:37.760
You're well-educated. Didn't they teach you

329
10:37.760 --> 10:40.210
not to bend over so much when you work? It's bad for your posture.

330
10:40.760 --> 10:41.730
Sit up straight.

331
10:41.730 --> 10:42.410
Ow...

332
10:43.390 --> 10:44.010
Whoa!

333
10:44.180 --> 10:44.720
Oh, wow!

334
10:44.860 --> 10:46.580
Is that an amulet or a church tile? So big.

335
10:46.730 --> 10:47.640
This is Venerable Father Song's amulet.

336
10:48.010 --> 10:49.390
I think that's an entire choir.

337
10:49.390 --> 10:50.590
Very grand.

338
10:51.010 --> 10:51.880
It's not!

339
10:52.950 --> 10:55.160
He gave me a smaller amulet at first.

340
10:55.160 --> 10:55.740
But...

341
10:55.980 --> 10:57.060
I felt uneasy,

342
10:57.370 --> 10:58.990
so I asked him for the limited edition.

343
10:59.340 --> 11:00.650
I don't wanna brag...

344
11:00.650 --> 11:01.390
I don't wanna listen, either.

345
11:01.730 --> 11:02.890
- Please do. - Alright.

346
11:03.410 --> 11:04.540
The previous owner,

347
11:04.760 --> 11:05.340
Grandma Tim.

348
11:05.340 --> 11:05.700
Mm.

349
11:05.900 --> 11:07.620
She went on a cruise.

350
11:07.800 --> 11:08.840
A storm hit,

351
11:08.940 --> 11:10.290
and the ship sank.

352
11:10.290 --> 11:10.990
She survived?

353
11:10.990 --> 11:11.820
She was the first to die.

354
11:11.820 --> 11:12.440
- It's this heavy. - Huh?

355
11:13.140 --> 11:14.420
After Grandma Tim passed,

356
11:14.420 --> 11:15.120
the amulet was still there.

357
11:15.120 --> 11:15.530
Whoa.

358
11:15.530 --> 11:17.150
It went to its second owner, Grandma Toi.

359
11:17.240 --> 11:17.760
Whoa.

360
11:17.760 --> 11:19.390
Grandma Toi was terminally ill,

361
11:19.390 --> 11:20.760
- Mm. - so she got this amulet.

362
11:20.760 --> 11:21.790
She complained every day,

363
11:21.790 --> 11:23.330
"I really, really want to die."

364
11:23.330 --> 11:23.720
Mm.

365
11:23.740 --> 11:25.070
Would you believe that within seven days...

366
11:25.090 --> 11:26.220
She got better?

367
11:26.220 --> 11:27.330
She died, just as she'd asked.

368
11:27.330 --> 11:28.000
Huh?

369
11:28.200 --> 11:28.690
But

370
11:28.690 --> 11:29.720
the amulet is still here, see?

371
11:30.060 --> 11:31.040
Take it off.

372
11:31.040 --> 11:32.000
Hey, don't.

373
11:32.120 --> 11:33.660
- I feel safer like this. - Take it off...

374
11:33.660 --> 11:34.600
Just take it off. Don't...

375
11:34.730 --> 11:35.680
Are you really gonna do it?

376
11:35.680 --> 11:36.440
Yes, take it off already.

377
11:36.690 --> 11:38.020
You look funny with that.

378
11:38.700 --> 11:39.620
Ugh, I'm getting goosebumps.

379
11:40.440 --> 11:41.360
Hey, Daeng.

380
11:41.360 --> 11:42.050
Seriously,

381
11:42.050 --> 11:43.820
did you really see Gramps' ghost?

382
11:44.140 --> 11:45.620
Why would I lie to you?

383
11:47.290 --> 11:49.080
This is the second time I've seen him.

384
11:50.280 --> 11:51.790
When I'm with Dawin,

385
11:52.020 --> 11:53.410
I always see ghosts.

386
11:55.780 --> 11:56.410
Guard Dum,

387
11:57.130 --> 11:58.410
- I have something to ask. - Yes?

388
11:59.180 --> 12:00.400
Have you ever seen...

389
12:00.760 --> 12:02.590
the guy from room 201?

390
12:03.490 --> 12:04.000
Oh,

391
12:04.290 --> 12:04.760
I have.

392
12:04.760 --> 12:06.040
He moved in recently.

393
12:06.300 --> 12:06.960
Why do you ask?

394
12:07.580 --> 12:08.400
Did you...

395
12:09.600 --> 12:12.720
see him acting suspiciously, too?

396
12:13.390 --> 12:14.410
- Hey... - "Too"?

397
12:15.280 --> 12:16.410
You saw it, too?

398
12:17.820 --> 12:18.410
Quite a lot, actually.

399
12:20.730 --> 12:22.420
The first day he moved in,

400
12:23.360 --> 12:25.060
I helped him carry his belongings.

401
12:25.060 --> 12:25.720
Oops!

402
12:26.080 --> 12:26.590
Ow.

403
12:28.810 --> 12:29.920
There was a human skull...

404
12:30.190 --> 12:31.760
in his box.

405
12:39.020 --> 12:40.260
And at night,

406
12:40.860 --> 12:41.740
he often...

407
12:42.410 --> 12:44.590
passed some kind of pot

408
12:44.820 --> 12:46.990
sealed with red cloth to someone.

409
12:47.720 --> 12:49.130
The person who got the pot

410
12:49.390 --> 12:50.400
called him...

411
12:50.770 --> 12:51.790
"Master," too.

412
12:55.020 --> 12:55.970
The most recent one

413
12:56.760 --> 12:57.790
was a few days ago.

414
12:58.280 --> 12:59.160
My brother

415
12:59.560 --> 13:00.900
wanted to check the grout in his bathroom.

416
13:00.900 --> 13:01.980
- He wouldn't - That's right.

417
13:02.440 --> 13:04.060
let us inside no matter what.

418
13:05.220 --> 13:06.190
Yes, yes.

419
13:07.010 --> 13:07.770
That day,

420
13:08.280 --> 13:09.410
I went to knock on his door.

421
13:09.410 --> 13:10.990
Knock, knock, knock, knock.

422
13:11.220 --> 13:12.190
But he didn't answer.

423
13:12.720 --> 13:14.400
So I tried to listen...

424
13:15.090 --> 13:16.410
I heard some kind of...

425
13:18.190 --> 13:19.680
chanting

426
13:19.810 --> 13:20.590
coming from inside.

427
13:22.120 --> 13:22.650
That's right.

428
13:23.180 --> 13:25.040
If I remember correctly, it was...

429
13:25.800 --> 13:26.280
Om...

430
13:26.280 --> 13:29.580
Bingle, bongle, dingle, dangle,

431
13:29.580 --> 13:32.590
yikketee-doo, yikketee-da,

432
13:32.590 --> 13:34.280
ping-pong lippy-tappy too-ta...

433
13:34.280 --> 13:35.340
- Bam! Bam! Bam! - Bam! Bam! Bam!

434
13:35.340 --> 13:36.420
Hey!

435
13:36.640 --> 13:37.970
Now is not the time to mess around.

436
13:38.130 --> 13:39.090
But you danced along.

437
13:39.120 --> 13:39.880
Well, I...

438
13:39.900 --> 13:40.810
I couldn't help it.

439
13:41.460 --> 13:42.190
Handyman Daeng,

440
13:42.650 --> 13:44.420
do you happen to have a spare key to his room?

441
13:44.590 --> 13:45.410
Room 201.

442
13:46.420 --> 13:47.180
I do.

443
13:47.780 --> 13:48.440
But...

444
13:49.000 --> 13:50.410
what are you going to do with it?

445
13:53.970 --> 13:55.180
[Beware of outsiders trying to steal your belongings,

446
13:55.200 --> 13:56.090
as thieves are on the rampage lately]

447
13:57.900 --> 13:58.680
Oh,

448
13:59.120 --> 14:00.940
I think he might be the thief

449
14:00.940 --> 14:03.280
who's been stealing from tenants in this dorm.

450
14:04.250 --> 14:04.960
Huh?

451
14:06.530 --> 14:07.190
That's right.

452
14:07.250 --> 14:08.890
I need to...

453
14:09.170 --> 14:11.620
find some evidence from his room.

454
14:12.410 --> 14:13.980
Can you two help me out?

455
14:22.240 --> 14:24.790
[Duangjai's Kitchen, Made-to-Order Food]

456
14:25.140 --> 14:26.300
Auntie Duang,

457
14:26.380 --> 14:27.970
I'm here to pick up the food I ordered.

458
14:28.040 --> 14:29.250
It's on the table.

459
14:29.250 --> 14:29.700
Oh...

460
14:30.190 --> 14:31.280
Did you find it?

461
14:32.260 --> 14:32.570
Yes, that one.

462
14:32.590 --> 14:33.420
Fudge!

463
14:33.790 --> 14:34.760
What fudge?

464
14:34.760 --> 14:36.190
You scared me.

465
14:36.190 --> 14:38.060
You're dressed like the Ring Nebula.

466
14:38.060 --> 14:39.130
The Ring Nebula...

467
14:39.130 --> 14:40.200
Is that something like...

468
14:40.200 --> 14:41.780
the Kanchanaphisek Ring Road?

469
14:42.960 --> 14:43.920
No,

470
14:43.920 --> 14:45.280
the Ring Nebula

471
14:45.600 --> 14:49.160
was formed from the ejected outer layers of gas around a star.

472
14:49.160 --> 14:50.400
It is also known as

473
14:50.400 --> 14:52.020
M5...

474
14:52.020 --> 14:52.720
Enough!

475
14:52.720 --> 14:53.690
I don't wanna hear it.

476
14:54.880 --> 14:55.920
By the way,

477
14:56.100 --> 14:56.940
- you... - Yes?

478
14:57.160 --> 14:59.770
shouldn't be questioning what I'm wearing.

479
15:02.010 --> 15:03.140
I'm wearing

480
15:03.990 --> 15:05.730
my lucky clothes.

481
15:05.730 --> 15:06.190
Okay.

482
15:06.560 --> 15:07.390
Blue...

483
15:07.650 --> 15:08.850
gives you money.

484
15:09.790 --> 15:10.570
Orange...

485
15:10.570 --> 15:11.900
grants you wealth.

486
15:12.330 --> 15:13.090
Red...

487
15:13.090 --> 15:14.300
threatens your enemies.

488
15:15.580 --> 15:16.450
Pink...

489
15:16.450 --> 15:17.700
improves your health.

490
15:18.080 --> 15:18.920
Yellow...

491
15:19.180 --> 15:20.240
for a flow of wisdom.

492
15:20.240 --> 15:21.040
So?

493
15:21.040 --> 15:22.990
Time to go to a psych ward!

494
15:22.990 --> 15:24.330
Bye-bye.

495
15:25.280 --> 15:26.180
Bye-bye.

496
15:26.590 --> 15:27.290
What?

497
15:27.290 --> 15:27.790
Mom, what is it?

498
15:27.790 --> 15:29.040
I've already been feeling unlucky lately.

499
15:29.130 --> 15:31.250
It was a joke, Mom.

500
15:31.250 --> 15:32.980
Please don't get mad, Mrs. Duangjai.

501
15:33.290 --> 15:36.450
You realize what a good son you have, yeah?

502
15:36.820 --> 15:38.260
- Good, my foot. You little brat. - Oh, huh?

503
15:39.340 --> 15:40.700
Dolly, what did you do to my face?

504
15:40.700 --> 15:41.800
- Mom! - What did you do?

505
15:41.800 --> 15:42.450
Wait, wait.

506
15:43.720 --> 15:45.470
What did you draw on your brother's face?

507
15:47.300 --> 15:48.720
You were the one who told me

508
15:48.720 --> 15:50.210
if I wanted to know what Dad looks like,

509
15:50.230 --> 15:51.990
just draw a mustache on him.

510
15:52.010 --> 15:52.560
What?

511
15:52.590 --> 15:53.200
There.

512
15:54.690 --> 15:55.660
By the way...

513
15:56.130 --> 15:57.440
Did I get the style right?

514
15:57.440 --> 15:58.990
Mm...

515
15:59.640 --> 16:01.440
If not, I can wipe it out and draw a new one.

516
16:02.590 --> 16:04.380
The old one is still on my face. You wanna draw more?

517
16:04.380 --> 16:04.990
You...

518
16:05.120 --> 16:06.050
- Should I draw on your face, too? Huh? - Whoa.

519
16:06.050 --> 16:07.100
- Should I do yours, too? - These two...

520
16:07.100 --> 16:08.160
- Want me to draw it on you, too? - only fight...

521
16:08.360 --> 16:09.530
- when it comes to their father! - Let go of me.

522
16:09.530 --> 16:10.420
- Let go... Let me go. - Ouch!

523
16:10.420 --> 16:10.990
Stop...

524
16:10.990 --> 16:11.920
Boys, enough.

525
16:11.920 --> 16:12.640
Please.

526
16:12.640 --> 16:13.390
- Mom, stay out of it. - Mom.

527
16:13.390 --> 16:14.000
- Mom, help me. - Give me...

528
16:14.000 --> 16:14.360
Mom...

529
16:14.360 --> 16:14.940
- Mom. - Mom, don't...

530
16:15.380 --> 16:16.020
- Mom! - It's gone.

531
16:16.020 --> 16:16.620
Give it to me.

532
16:17.200 --> 16:19.990
It would be nice if Dolly could see his father for once...

533
16:20.360 --> 16:21.040
- Mom, please. - Mom, Mom.

534
16:21.040 --> 16:22.620
- Mom, stay out of it. - Mom... Mom!

535
16:22.620 --> 16:22.880
Dear...

536
16:22.880 --> 16:23.930
- Dolly, let go! - Ow!

537
16:25.240 --> 16:26.260
Stop... Please.

538
16:26.590 --> 16:27.450
Dollar!

539
16:30.700 --> 16:31.760
Stop... Stop.

540
16:32.590 --> 16:33.420
I'm not letting go.

541
16:33.420 --> 16:34.040
Mom...

542
16:34.040 --> 16:34.990
- Mom, it's slipping out. - Stop...

543
16:47.800 --> 16:48.970
Why hasn't he come out yet?

544
16:49.930 --> 16:50.400
Ow!

545
16:50.780 --> 16:51.260
Oops.

546
16:51.790 --> 16:52.440
I'm sorry.

547
16:52.820 --> 16:53.410
Wow...

548
16:53.410 --> 16:54.740
Your forehead sounds quite solid,

549
16:54.740 --> 16:55.850
like one of those Jintara watermelons.

550
16:57.410 --> 16:58.050
What is it?

551
16:58.480 --> 17:01.920
Are you Mr. Don, the owner of the car with the license plate 1331?

552
17:02.590 --> 17:03.120
I am.

553
17:03.440 --> 17:04.220
There are some issues with your car.

554
17:04.220 --> 17:05.380
We need to go check it out right away.

555
17:06.440 --> 17:07.390
What happened to my car?

556
17:09.410 --> 17:10.359
Uh...

557
17:10.359 --> 17:13.390
I did a quick check just now...

558
17:13.390 --> 17:14.180
- Right. - Oh...

559
17:14.420 --> 17:15.790
- It's pretty severe. - It is.

560
17:16.000 --> 17:18.540
It would be best if you went to see it yourself.

561
17:18.540 --> 17:19.740
Yes, it's severe.

562
17:19.740 --> 17:20.369
Mm.

563
17:28.730 --> 17:30.040
Your forehead sounds quite solid,

564
17:30.480 --> 17:31.710
like one of those Long and Lin durians.

565
17:33.320 --> 17:34.440
Did you take a peek inside my room?

566
17:37.840 --> 17:39.640
I noticed that your room was red.

567
17:39.640 --> 17:41.570
Red is my favorite color...

568
17:41.570 --> 17:44.420
I wanted to know if the room would be beautifully decorated.

569
17:44.800 --> 17:46.280
He loves red. His brother "Daeng" means red...

570
17:46.280 --> 17:47.610
How I decorate my room

571
17:48.300 --> 17:49.440
is none of your concern.

572
17:49.520 --> 17:50.460
How could you say that?

573
17:50.700 --> 17:51.790
My head still hurts even now.

574
17:51.970 --> 17:53.210
It obviously concerns me.

575
17:53.530 --> 17:54.240
After you.

576
17:56.800 --> 17:57.770
After...

577
17:57.790 --> 17:59.410
- Daeng, Daeng, Daeng, help me out. - Oh.

578
18:01.530 --> 18:03.450
This way.

579
18:03.450 --> 18:04.250
Go downstairs.

580
18:04.250 --> 18:04.990
Oh, wow...

581
18:06.700 --> 18:07.760
They're leaving.

582
18:16.520 --> 18:17.660
Hey, wait.

583
18:17.660 --> 18:18.190
What?

584
18:18.330 --> 18:19.940
If this really is a shaman's room,

585
18:20.730 --> 18:21.790
we can't be too careful.

586
18:22.940 --> 18:24.810
A kuman thong might be targeting us.

587
18:25.390 --> 18:26.120
What should we do, then?

588
18:26.770 --> 18:27.220
Look.

589
18:31.250 --> 18:33.520
Let's play! Let's play!

590
18:33.790 --> 18:34.740
Let's play.

591
18:45.340 --> 18:46.220
Whoa...

592
18:46.410 --> 18:47.420
He's gone now.

593
18:48.770 --> 18:49.700
It's gone now, yeah.

594
18:49.700 --> 18:50.590
You mean the kuman thong?

595
18:50.970 --> 18:52.010
Your braincells.

596
18:52.220 --> 18:52.990
They are all gone.

597
18:52.990 --> 18:53.730
Hey...

598
18:53.730 --> 18:54.930
- Ugh, this is stupid. - You're being mean again...

599
18:58.990 --> 19:00.190
Hide inside.

600
19:16.850 --> 19:17.540
Whoa...

601
19:18.050 --> 19:18.740
Whoa...

602
19:29.280 --> 19:29.770
Whoa...

603
19:30.570 --> 19:31.700
All these pots...

604
19:31.950 --> 19:34.100
If he wasn't a shaman, he'd make a great hot pot restaurant owner.

605
19:37.390 --> 19:37.860
Hey,

606
19:38.480 --> 19:39.790
why are there only empty pots here?

607
19:40.760 --> 19:41.970
If Grandpa's ghost was really in there,

608
19:42.490 --> 19:43.800
there must be a red talisman over it, right?

609
19:45.180 --> 19:45.790
You're right.

610
19:46.720 --> 19:47.400
Where is it, then?

611
20:00.000 --> 20:00.500
Dax.

612
20:00.500 --> 20:01.040
Whoa.

613
20:01.520 --> 20:02.450
It's chained up.

614
20:05.970 --> 20:06.570
Hey...

615
20:06.770 --> 20:07.720
Move, move, move.

616
20:19.260 --> 20:20.590
So, what's wrong with my car?

617
20:21.680 --> 20:25.390
Well, our dorm has a new rule.

618
20:25.900 --> 20:28.090
Every tenant with a natural gas car

619
20:28.090 --> 20:30.970
must receive a safety training course

620
20:30.970 --> 20:32.640
hosted by me.

621
20:32.780 --> 20:33.450
Huh?!

622
20:34.000 --> 20:34.740
What training course?

623
20:34.880 --> 20:38.940
Without further ado, let's begin our safety training course

624
20:38.940 --> 20:41.180
for natural gas car owners!

625
20:44.820 --> 20:46.640
To ensure safety for all tenants,

626
20:46.880 --> 20:49.010
please follow these five Ds.

627
20:49.010 --> 20:50.020
The first D.

628
20:50.300 --> 20:52.040
Do a sniff test before you start the car

629
20:52.040 --> 20:53.440
in case there is a gas leak.

630
20:57.130 --> 20:57.790
What?

631
21:00.900 --> 21:01.820
What?

632
21:03.320 --> 21:04.160
A gas leak!

633
21:05.210 --> 21:06.400
The second D.

634
21:06.770 --> 21:09.540
Do fasten your seatbelt before driving.

635
21:15.680 --> 21:16.990
I said fasten your seatbelt, not fishing.

636
21:16.990 --> 21:18.190
I have to pull it over my belly.

637
21:19.760 --> 21:20.590
In case...

638
21:20.860 --> 21:21.440
the gas explodes.

639
21:21.440 --> 21:22.410
Boom!

640
21:22.990 --> 21:24.580
It will be easier to find your body.

641
21:29.620 --> 21:30.400
Everything remains intact.

642
21:32.060 --> 21:32.920
What even is this?

643
21:32.920 --> 21:33.790
This is ridiculous.

644
21:34.530 --> 21:35.480
How is this ridiculous?

645
21:35.480 --> 21:36.190
Come here.

646
21:37.580 --> 21:39.080
Sit here and you might understand it better.

647
21:40.020 --> 21:41.840
Safety measures must not be overlooked.

648
21:44.920 --> 21:46.220
Sorry, but this is a car, not a bus.

649
21:46.220 --> 21:47.450
- Why are you holding the handle? - I'm sorry.

650
21:48.190 --> 21:49.280
The third D.

651
21:49.280 --> 21:51.660
Do read dhamma books regularly,

652
21:51.660 --> 21:52.990
so you become more mindful

653
21:53.220 --> 21:55.390
and remain calm when you drive.

654
21:56.010 --> 21:57.450
Screech!

655
22:00.840 --> 22:01.690
Excuse me,

656
22:02.090 --> 22:03.300
why did you cut me off?

657
22:03.790 --> 22:04.990
I have a car insurance.

658
22:08.360 --> 22:09.110
Sorry?

659
22:09.340 --> 22:10.400
Oh, we're Thai people.

660
22:10.530 --> 22:12.010
Let's greet one another with a warm hello,

661
22:12.190 --> 22:14.140
instead of a middle finger.

662
22:17.850 --> 22:18.730
Yes?

663
22:18.730 --> 22:19.390
My mom?

664
22:20.410 --> 22:21.240
I only have one mother.

665
22:21.240 --> 22:22.540
Not six nor seven.

666
22:22.990 --> 22:23.760
Yes.

667
22:25.220 --> 22:26.130
This is nonsense.

668
22:26.130 --> 22:27.380
Such a waste of my time.

669
22:27.380 --> 22:28.440
Where are you going? The car is moving!

670
22:28.440 --> 22:28.990
Oh, right.

671
22:29.740 --> 22:30.460
- Hey! - What?

672
22:30.780 --> 22:31.900
You got me there.

673
22:33.790 --> 22:34.990
- What? - What should we do?

674
22:35.100 --> 22:36.980
His patience ran out after only three Ds.

675
22:37.140 --> 22:40.100
We don't know if those two Ds have found any evidence yet.

676
22:40.300 --> 22:41.340
They definitely don't have enough time.

677
22:41.340 --> 22:42.190
We have to stall him.

678
22:42.880 --> 22:43.250
Mm.

679
22:44.720 --> 22:45.400
Mr. Don,

680
22:45.900 --> 22:46.990
if you want to skip the course,

681
22:46.990 --> 22:48.500
you'll have to prove that your car

682
22:48.500 --> 22:50.590
is safe for the sake of our tenants.

683
22:50.590 --> 22:51.650
Prove what now?

684
22:51.650 --> 22:53.290
You've wasted enough of my time.

685
22:54.190 --> 22:55.080
We only ask for a moment.

686
22:55.390 --> 22:56.140
It won't take long.

687
22:57.460 --> 22:58.210
We'll take a look at your D.

688
22:58.210 --> 22:58.990
Whoa!

689
22:59.400 --> 23:00.190
We'll take a look at your "destiny."

690
23:01.240 --> 23:02.200
You scared me.

691
23:02.450 --> 23:03.340
It's an abbreviation, alright?

692
23:09.910 --> 23:10.670
Whoa!

693
23:11.450 --> 23:12.650
You're the real deal, huh?

694
23:13.650 --> 23:14.740
Where did you learn this from?

695
23:14.740 --> 23:15.360
I learned it...

696
23:15.360 --> 23:17.580
when I starred in 'Tawan Tud Burapa Withi.'

697
23:18.370 --> 23:19.390
You mean 'Tawan Tud Burapa'?

698
23:19.390 --> 23:20.250
This is the sequel.

699
23:20.450 --> 23:22.990
The lead died while he was driving on Burapha Withi Expressway.

700
23:22.990 --> 23:24.500
He was shot. Bang! Bang! Bang!

701
23:24.500 --> 23:25.280
A bunch of bullet holes.

702
23:25.280 --> 23:26.590
Whoa... That doesn't sound like a good movie.

703
23:27.240 --> 23:27.640
It is good, though.

704
23:27.640 --> 23:28.260
Yeah, whatever.

705
23:28.260 --> 23:28.850
Go!

706
23:43.640 --> 23:44.220
Dax,

707
23:44.840 --> 23:45.790
there are so many pots.

708
23:47.320 --> 23:48.190
Grandpa.

709
23:49.210 --> 23:49.960
Grandpa?

710
23:50.250 --> 23:50.970
Grandpa...

711
23:51.680 --> 23:52.400
- Dax... - Whoa.

712
23:53.240 --> 23:54.190
Grandpa isn't answering.

713
23:57.080 --> 23:57.580
I'll...

714
23:57.580 --> 23:58.530
open every single one, then.

715
23:58.530 --> 23:59.610
Hey, wait, Dobby.

716
23:59.820 --> 24:00.190
Huh?

717
24:00.890 --> 24:01.850
If you opened them all,

718
24:02.590 --> 24:03.570
the D Dorm

719
24:03.790 --> 24:04.990
would turn into Disneyland's Haunted Mansion.

720
24:06.580 --> 24:07.440
What should we do, then?

721
24:09.080 --> 24:09.790
Hey...

722
24:10.000 --> 24:10.410
Hm?

723
24:10.680 --> 24:11.700
You're Gramps' grandson.

724
24:13.100 --> 24:14.120
You have to use this.

725
24:14.960 --> 24:15.520
Here.

726
24:20.280 --> 24:20.720
My nipple?

727
24:20.720 --> 24:21.300
Ugh...

728
24:21.560 --> 24:22.260
Your heart!

729
24:23.210 --> 24:24.190
Oh, my heart.

730
24:24.190 --> 24:25.120
- Yeah. - Mm.

731
24:25.700 --> 24:26.590
Listen.

732
24:27.020 --> 24:27.380
Yeah?

733
24:27.980 --> 24:29.700
Back when I was studying acting,

734
24:31.010 --> 24:32.220
I learned that you could tell

735
24:33.130 --> 24:34.680
what color the other person was thinking of

736
24:34.990 --> 24:36.440
just by holding hands with them.

737
24:38.410 --> 24:39.680
Try to focus.

738
24:39.680 --> 24:40.160
Mm.

739
24:40.160 --> 24:41.250
Think of Gramps.

740
24:43.050 --> 24:44.590
You might be able to sense his presence.

741
24:46.010 --> 24:46.690
That...

742
24:46.990 --> 24:47.560
is...

743
24:48.190 --> 24:48.890
possible...

744
24:49.390 --> 24:50.260
Thank you, Ryu.

745
24:51.330 --> 24:51.790
It's Dax!

746
24:52.370 --> 24:52.990
Oh, Dax.

747
24:52.990 --> 24:53.730
- Mm. - Alright.

748
25:10.140 --> 25:12.330
Are you hiding a secret?

749
25:15.680 --> 25:16.780
The cards are telling me that...

750
25:17.420 --> 25:20.020
you're covering up a mistake.

751
25:20.960 --> 25:22.220
And the rotten filth

752
25:22.740 --> 25:24.190
you've been hiding

753
25:24.500 --> 25:25.570
will be exposed in no time.

754
25:28.140 --> 25:28.820
Mr. Don,

755
25:28.970 --> 25:30.620
are you really hiding something?

756
25:31.580 --> 25:32.820
Whatever it is that I'm hiding

757
25:33.060 --> 25:34.420
is none of your concern.

758
25:36.060 --> 25:37.390
But the cards told me.

759
25:38.280 --> 25:40.990
You're breaking the law,

760
25:41.410 --> 25:42.560
the law of nature.

761
25:43.760 --> 25:44.590
Enough of this!

762
25:44.590 --> 25:45.920
- This is stupid. I'm going back to my room. - Hey! Sit down!

763
25:46.040 --> 25:46.990
Don't go!

764
25:48.530 --> 25:49.620
You can't leave yet.

765
25:49.620 --> 25:51.440
If you insist on skipping the course,

766
25:51.440 --> 25:52.700
you'll have to see the D!

767
25:52.700 --> 25:53.380
- Huh? - Destiny.

768
25:53.980 --> 25:54.440
Oh,

769
25:54.440 --> 25:55.170
a reading of your destiny!

770
25:55.950 --> 25:56.660
Don't try to stop me!

771
25:56.680 --> 25:57.200
Sit!

772
25:57.200 --> 25:57.790
Stop.

773
25:57.790 --> 25:58.420
Sit down.

774
25:59.370 --> 26:00.620
If you want to stay safe,

775
26:00.620 --> 26:01.390
sit down,

776
26:01.530 --> 26:02.960
and let the cards guide you.

777
26:03.980 --> 26:04.820
Daeng the Handyman, hold him still!

778
26:04.820 --> 26:05.250
Hey,

779
26:07.120 --> 26:07.940
stop it!

780
26:08.180 --> 26:09.140
Don't forget your promise

781
26:09.140 --> 26:11.480
that you'll help me hold hands with your brother.

782
26:11.480 --> 26:12.190
Ugh, alright.

783
26:12.190 --> 26:13.390
Why are you nagging me so much?

784
26:13.390 --> 26:14.420
Try to stop him first.

785
26:15.240 --> 26:16.420
You won't let me go, huh?

786
26:17.370 --> 26:18.440
Hey, he's going to use black magic!

787
26:18.440 --> 26:19.020
- Whoa. - Whoa.

788
26:19.200 --> 26:20.850
Hey... What is he doing?

789
26:21.050 --> 26:21.790
- Stand back. - Whoa.

790
26:23.920 --> 26:25.240
He might be a master thief

791
26:25.240 --> 26:26.400
who practices black magic,

792
26:26.650 --> 26:27.680
but don't worry,

793
26:27.680 --> 26:29.430
I know a few tricks that can protect us.

794
26:31.810 --> 26:32.590
You want some of this?

795
26:34.090 --> 26:34.370
Ow!

796
26:34.640 --> 26:34.990
Ow!

797
26:39.560 --> 26:40.120
What's wrong?

798
26:40.660 --> 26:42.020
It hurts, obviously.

799
26:42.020 --> 26:43.200
- Try again. - Give it another try.

800
26:43.200 --> 26:44.170
Ohm... Tapati Tapata...

801
26:44.170 --> 26:45.340
- What now?! - Ouch!

802
26:45.340 --> 26:46.450
Ugh, I'm leaving.

803
26:46.620 --> 26:47.220
Whoa.

804
26:48.730 --> 26:49.390
Ow!

805
26:52.220 --> 26:54.190
[The D Dorm]

806
26:54.800 --> 26:55.650
Grandpa.

807
26:57.200 --> 26:57.940
Grandpa...

808
26:59.620 --> 27:01.180
If you can hear me,

809
27:01.180 --> 27:02.590
please say something.

810
27:03.790 --> 27:04.780
Vroom, vroom.

811
27:06.930 --> 27:07.580
Grandpa?

812
27:07.690 --> 27:08.590
Are you driving?

813
27:09.370 --> 27:10.120
Grandpa...

814
27:11.850 --> 27:13.180
- To the left, to the left. - Dax!

815
27:13.850 --> 27:14.840
- Go that way... - Dax,

816
27:14.840 --> 27:16.180
what the hell are you doing? Get in here!

817
27:18.190 --> 27:19.570
What were you doing?

818
27:20.240 --> 27:20.760
Huh?

819
27:23.450 --> 27:24.190
Yeah, Guard Dum?

820
27:25.060 --> 27:25.920
- Huh?! - Hah?!

821
27:26.510 --> 27:27.410
Don is on his way back here?

822
27:27.410 --> 27:28.120
What?

823
27:33.260 --> 27:34.990
Who put this R/C car here?

824
27:45.900 --> 27:47.400
What was that all about...?

825
27:50.920 --> 27:51.640
Huh?!

826
27:52.370 --> 27:53.400
Who's in here?!

827
27:55.080 --> 27:56.030
Show yourself!

828
28:05.250 --> 28:05.930
Come on out!

829
28:09.790 --> 28:10.660
Keep quiet...

830
28:16.990 --> 28:18.190
You're in there, huh?

831
28:30.350 --> 28:31.550
They must be in here...

832
28:46.040 --> 28:46.760
Hello?

833
28:46.990 --> 28:47.840
Gramps?

834
28:49.690 --> 28:51.110
I handled that already.

835
28:52.740 --> 28:53.250
Dobby...

836
28:53.810 --> 28:54.730
He's talking about Gramps.

837
28:54.940 --> 28:55.780
I heard that.

838
28:57.940 --> 28:59.100
Oh, you've arrived?

839
29:00.400 --> 29:01.810
I'll bring it to you myself.

840
29:11.450 --> 29:13.020
This ends here, Gramps.

841
29:13.570 --> 29:14.250
Grandpa.

842
29:18.600 --> 29:19.390
Stop right there.

843
29:19.810 --> 29:21.080
- Whoa. - Give me back my grandpa!

844
29:21.080 --> 29:22.280
Hey, how did you get in here?!

845
29:22.450 --> 29:23.140
You're evil.

846
29:23.140 --> 29:24.540
How dare you take his grandpa away from him?

847
29:24.540 --> 29:25.700
What are you saying?!

848
29:25.700 --> 29:26.940
- Don't try to act innocent. Give him back to me! - Hey!

849
29:26.940 --> 29:28.000
- Ow. - Ouch.

850
29:28.140 --> 29:28.680
Hey!

851
29:31.540 --> 29:32.530
Hey, stop right there!

852
29:33.790 --> 29:34.990
- Stop it, you thief. - Stop.

853
29:35.170 --> 29:36.190
What thief?!

854
29:36.190 --> 29:37.120
Hey, stop.

855
29:37.640 --> 29:38.440
Whoa, whoa.

856
29:41.420 --> 29:42.700
Give me back Grandpa's pot.

857
29:42.700 --> 29:43.750
Never!

858
29:45.940 --> 29:47.040
Don't try to run away.

859
29:50.930 --> 29:51.440
Whoa!

860
29:54.850 --> 29:55.650
Whoa, Dax.

861
29:56.120 --> 29:56.740
- Whoa. - Whoa.

862
29:58.450 --> 29:58.990
Whoa.

863
30:02.720 --> 30:03.790
Let go!

864
30:04.240 --> 30:05.320
No... I won't.

865
30:05.320 --> 30:05.970
Let go...

866
30:06.190 --> 30:06.890
No.

867
30:06.890 --> 30:07.390
Let go.

868
30:07.970 --> 30:09.060
Give me the pot!

869
30:09.360 --> 30:10.200
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

870
30:10.800 --> 30:12.190
How about Virgil van Dijk's defending style?

871
30:22.140 --> 30:22.770
What?

872
30:26.840 --> 30:27.480
- Ouch! - Hey.

873
30:28.200 --> 30:29.050
Virgil van Dijk is now exhausted!

874
30:29.100 --> 30:30.190
This is why Liverpool wasn't the champion!

875
30:30.190 --> 30:31.440
Ow, that hurts...

876
30:32.590 --> 30:33.460
- Hey. - Don't try to run away.

877
30:34.180 --> 30:34.990
- Oh! - Give me that.

878
30:40.580 --> 30:41.770
Whoa!

879
30:47.740 --> 30:49.640
Whoa...

880
30:52.680 --> 30:54.420
Grandpa!

881
31:02.730 --> 31:04.180
This is fermented fish!

882
31:05.840 --> 31:08.700
What are you doing?!

883
31:17.200 --> 31:17.960
Hey, Mr. Don,

884
31:18.190 --> 31:20.590
have you been making and selling fermented fish here in this dorm?

885
31:22.210 --> 31:22.990
I'm sorry.

886
31:23.470 --> 31:26.400
[Don, occupation: (fermented fish) seller]

887
31:26.860 --> 31:27.790
If you were making fermented fish,

888
31:28.370 --> 31:30.190
then why is your room full of sacred items?

889
31:30.190 --> 31:31.390
You were acting like a shaman, even.

890
31:32.100 --> 31:34.320
Well... I wanted my brand to stand out.

891
31:34.640 --> 31:36.440
And my friend said that

892
31:36.440 --> 31:38.510
I looked like Master from 'Khemjira The Series.'

893
31:39.300 --> 31:40.720
So I turned that idea...

894
31:40.960 --> 31:41.810
into Master's fermented fish.

895
31:41.810 --> 31:43.020
- Whoa. - Hmm.

896
31:43.020 --> 31:44.260
There are many other series to choose from,

897
31:44.410 --> 31:45.240
why this one?

898
31:45.570 --> 31:47.290
Well, I like it.

899
31:47.330 --> 31:49.690
And what I like is none of your concern.

900
31:50.010 --> 31:51.000
Ooh...

901
31:51.000 --> 31:52.050
Still feisty, huh?

902
31:52.050 --> 31:53.780
He's probably telling you...

903
31:53.780 --> 31:54.620
to keep your nose out of this.

904
31:55.610 --> 31:57.980
I almost asked him if he also watched 'Your Third Series.'

905
31:58.990 --> 31:59.930
Don't forget to watch it as well.

906
32:00.580 --> 32:01.390
But wait,

907
32:01.980 --> 32:03.790
why did you call the pot "Gramps"?

908
32:03.950 --> 32:04.640
What does that mean?

909
32:06.150 --> 32:07.200
This fermented fish

910
32:07.200 --> 32:08.920
is my grandfather's recipe.

911
32:09.060 --> 32:10.990
I thought it didn't sell well,

912
32:11.140 --> 32:12.450
and there was only one pot left.

913
32:12.640 --> 32:14.020
I thought that I could sell it,

914
32:14.540 --> 32:16.370
but you guys spilled it before I could.

915
32:16.370 --> 32:17.240
Oh...

916
32:18.020 --> 32:19.170
Whoa, you're blaming us?

917
32:20.000 --> 32:21.650
You were being suspicious,

918
32:21.650 --> 32:23.080
so we thought you were a thief.

919
32:23.300 --> 32:23.940
Darn it...

920
32:24.640 --> 32:26.040
Do you practice black magic as well?

921
32:26.250 --> 32:27.790
When you picked up the prayer beads,

922
32:28.000 --> 32:29.280
I saw you mumbling

923
32:29.280 --> 32:30.700
as if you were chanting some incantation.

924
32:30.700 --> 32:31.350
Yeah.

925
32:32.000 --> 32:33.160
That wasn't an incantation.

926
32:33.460 --> 32:34.780
This was my mom's necklace.

927
32:36.190 --> 32:36.760
Mom,

928
32:36.760 --> 32:37.940
I'll have to borrow this necklace,

929
32:38.340 --> 32:39.400
and hit these people with it.

930
32:39.920 --> 32:40.990
Please don't get mad at me.

931
32:41.820 --> 32:42.190
Oh...

932
32:42.190 --> 32:43.390
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

933
32:43.390 --> 32:44.260
Ugh!

934
32:44.480 --> 32:45.160
Mr. Don,

935
32:45.310 --> 32:47.580
I'll have to warn you that

936
32:47.800 --> 32:50.010
if you keep making and selling fermented fish in this dorm,

937
32:50.010 --> 32:51.660
I won't let you stay here.

938
32:51.660 --> 32:52.770
It's against the rules.

939
32:53.180 --> 32:53.720
Uh...

940
32:53.720 --> 32:55.240
Then can I ditch the fish and sell

941
32:55.240 --> 32:56.840
fried insects instead?

942
32:56.840 --> 32:58.610
Lately, I've been into...

943
32:58.610 --> 32:59.560
Duang with You Series.'

944
32:59.560 --> 33:00.820
- Ugh... - Ugh.

945
33:00.820 --> 33:02.010
You only watch shows from one company, huh?

946
33:02.290 --> 33:03.370
Have you learned nothing?

947
33:03.540 --> 33:04.180
Ow...

948
33:04.860 --> 33:05.900
If your insects

949
33:05.900 --> 33:08.590
got out of the enclosure, what would you do?

950
33:08.610 --> 33:09.900
You talk a lot for someone who can't talk properly.

951
33:11.100 --> 33:12.700
You're injured but you keep running your mouth.

952
33:15.200 --> 33:16.130
Hey, Dobby.

953
33:16.690 --> 33:17.260
Huh?

954
33:20.120 --> 33:22.100
If this isn't the shaman Mr. Suraphon has sent,

955
33:22.620 --> 33:23.400
then who is he?

956
33:24.560 --> 33:25.660
I don't know either.

957
33:26.290 --> 33:27.420
I'm stressed out.

958
33:28.100 --> 33:29.300
Where did my grandpa go?

959
33:42.480 --> 33:43.880
Mom and Dad...

960
33:48.360 --> 33:50.590
Did you ever feel guilty

961
33:52.720 --> 33:54.410
when both of you

962
33:56.590 --> 33:58.740
forced me into an arranged marriage?

963
34:01.770 --> 34:02.880
Auntie,

964
34:03.000 --> 34:04.850
- I apologize on my son's behalf... - Shut up!

965
34:04.850 --> 34:05.480
You...

966
34:08.199 --> 34:09.440
Shut your stupid mouth.

967
34:09.790 --> 34:10.690
Keep your nose out of this.

968
34:15.790 --> 34:18.190
I was a deadbeat.

969
34:20.179 --> 34:22.080
A terrible father...

970
34:23.340 --> 34:25.800
I almost forced my daughter...

971
34:26.260 --> 34:28.409
to marry Surachet!

972
34:31.350 --> 34:33.100
If she had not run away,

973
34:36.210 --> 34:37.850
she would have had to marry him...

974
34:39.020 --> 34:40.100
She might have been

975
34:41.440 --> 34:43.940
living in hell right now...

976
34:56.739 --> 34:58.910
Danai Saeja!

977
34:59.260 --> 35:02.220
May you appear before me this instant.

978
35:02.220 --> 35:03.100
Who?!

979
35:03.580 --> 35:04.810
Who is calling me?!

980
35:07.390 --> 35:08.060
Who is it?!

981
35:08.060 --> 35:09.790
Danai Saeja,

982
35:10.140 --> 35:11.720
may you appear

983
35:11.750 --> 35:13.090
- before me... - What is happening to me?!

984
35:13.220 --> 35:14.810
this instant!

985
35:14.810 --> 35:15.790
What the hell is happening?

986
35:16.800 --> 35:18.210
Who is calling me?!

987
35:18.820 --> 35:19.540
Dobby.

988
35:19.540 --> 35:20.720
Danai Saeja!

989
35:20.720 --> 35:22.060
Dobby...

990
35:22.420 --> 35:24.720
- Dobby, help me. - May you appear

991
35:24.880 --> 35:26.260
before me...

992
35:26.590 --> 35:28.720
this instant!

993
35:30.720 --> 35:31.730
What should we do now?

994
35:31.930 --> 35:32.740
I don't know.

995
35:33.330 --> 35:35.320
Dobby!

996
35:35.320 --> 35:37.390
Help me!

997
35:37.780 --> 35:40.460
Dobby!

998
35:40.460 --> 35:40.990
Hey,

999
35:41.240 --> 35:42.700
Grandpa is calling for help.

1000
35:42.900 --> 35:43.680
Hey.

1001
35:44.340 --> 35:44.810
Whoa...

1002
35:46.990 --> 35:47.890
Have you finally arrived?

1003
35:47.890 --> 35:49.260
I feel very dizzy,

1004
35:49.260 --> 35:51.790
as if I went on a roller coaster.

1005
35:51.790 --> 35:52.820
It is time for you to

1006
35:52.820 --> 35:55.390
bid farewell to this dorm!

1007
35:55.390 --> 35:56.060
Whoa!

1008
35:58.360 --> 35:59.580
I don't get it, Mom.

1009
36:00.040 --> 36:01.390
Each time we fight,

1010
36:01.390 --> 36:03.680
why do I have to make up with Dolly by paying for his buffet?

1011
36:03.680 --> 36:04.740
Serves you right.

1012
36:04.740 --> 36:05.300
And look,

1013
36:05.300 --> 36:06.410
look at what you did to your brother.

1014
36:06.660 --> 36:07.200
Mm.

1015
36:10.990 --> 36:11.340
Hey.

1016
36:11.960 --> 36:12.890
Did you forget that

1017
36:13.050 --> 36:14.260
he was the one who started it?

1018
36:14.260 --> 36:15.640
- Oh. - Ugh...

1019
36:15.790 --> 36:17.420
I only drew a mustache, though?

1020
36:18.170 --> 36:19.040
But look at me.

1021
36:19.260 --> 36:21.180
You drew all over my face.

1022
36:21.650 --> 36:23.200
- Just saying it makes me angry. - And?

1023
36:23.200 --> 36:23.960
Give it to me...

1024
36:24.730 --> 36:25.880
Boys, stop...

1025
36:27.560 --> 36:28.540
- That's enough. - Let go.

1026
36:28.540 --> 36:29.450
- Let go. - Ow.

1027
36:29.450 --> 36:30.190
Let go already.

1028
36:30.480 --> 36:31.850
- Stop fighting! - Stop.

1029
36:31.850 --> 36:32.590
Dollar...

1030
36:32.590 --> 36:33.410
Let go, Dolly.

1031
36:33.410 --> 36:34.100
Let go.

1032
36:34.540 --> 36:35.530
- Stop this already. - Dolly, let go.

1033
36:35.700 --> 36:36.530
Ugh, boys!

1034
36:37.390 --> 36:38.590
That's enough.

1035
36:38.890 --> 36:39.790
- Whoa! - Huh!

1036
36:39.940 --> 36:40.560
Mom!

1037
36:40.560 --> 36:41.260
What happened?

1038
36:41.370 --> 36:42.380
You had to ask?

1039
36:42.760 --> 36:44.160
We're not going to that buffet anymore.

1040
36:44.380 --> 36:45.600
We're going to the salon

1041
36:45.600 --> 36:46.720
to wash all of this off.

1042
36:47.540 --> 36:48.620
- You... - Go!

1043
36:49.240 --> 36:49.930
Quickly!

1044
36:50.800 --> 36:51.440
- Oh. - Oh...

1045
36:51.580 --> 36:52.010
Whoa.

1046
36:52.010 --> 36:53.160
Whoa, Mom.

1047
36:53.160 --> 36:54.580
- He's so dramatic. - You have a problem with that?

1048
36:55.390 --> 36:56.000
Go!

1049
36:56.000 --> 36:58.450
Why did you draw a cross on my face? This isn't an election.

1050
37:22.130 --> 37:22.850
Who are you?

1051
37:22.850 --> 37:23.410
Oh!

1052
37:23.540 --> 37:24.960
What are you doing here?

1053
37:25.740 --> 37:26.590
I...

1054
37:27.020 --> 37:27.790
Uh...

1055
37:28.040 --> 37:28.640
I...

1056
37:29.460 --> 37:30.520
I came to see my relative.

1057
37:32.820 --> 37:34.230
My relative is the owner of this restaurant.

1058
37:34.990 --> 37:36.010
Wait.

1059
37:37.080 --> 37:39.480
Weren't you the one spying on Auntie Duang this afternoon?

1060
37:39.630 --> 37:40.620
Oh, oops...

1061
37:41.320 --> 37:42.690
You have a great memory, huh?

1062
37:42.690 --> 37:44.170
Uh, well...

1063
37:44.340 --> 37:45.050
I...

1064
37:45.050 --> 37:47.290
I'm here to surprise them.

1065
37:49.160 --> 37:49.840
Well,

1066
37:49.840 --> 37:50.590
I...

1067
37:50.770 --> 37:51.300
I...

1068
37:51.300 --> 37:52.820
haven't seen them in a long time.

1069
37:52.820 --> 37:53.980
So...

1070
37:54.190 --> 37:55.220
I wanted to...

1071
37:55.220 --> 37:56.320
I want this reunion...

1072
37:56.320 --> 37:57.520
to be something...

1073
37:57.520 --> 37:58.560
special.

1074
37:58.990 --> 37:59.580
Yeah.

1075
38:03.790 --> 38:05.200
You were the one who told me

1076
38:05.200 --> 38:06.660
if I wanted to know what Dad looks like,

1077
38:06.660 --> 38:08.410
just draw a mustache on him.

1078
38:14.330 --> 38:15.640
Don't tell me you are...

1079
38:16.810 --> 38:18.190
Auntie Duang's husband?

1080
38:18.500 --> 38:19.220
Whoa!

1081
38:21.570 --> 38:22.260
No, no, no, no.

1082
38:22.260 --> 38:22.990
That's wonderful.

1083
38:23.340 --> 38:24.890
Dolly will finally meet his father.

1084
38:25.850 --> 38:26.440
Shh.

1085
38:26.440 --> 38:27.440
Keep quiet.

1086
38:27.440 --> 38:28.810
Yeah, I'm his father.

1087
38:28.880 --> 38:30.410
That's great, isn't it?

1088
38:30.770 --> 38:33.250
Dolly's family will finally be reunited.

1089
38:33.790 --> 38:35.370
Let me call him.

1090
38:35.370 --> 38:37.000
Whoa, no! Stop!

1091
38:37.000 --> 38:37.740
Stop, stop.

1092
38:37.740 --> 38:38.240
Don't do that.

1093
38:38.540 --> 38:39.250
Don't call him.

1094
38:39.420 --> 38:40.450
Why not?

1095
38:40.990 --> 38:42.420
Well... Uh...

1096
38:43.170 --> 38:43.860
I...

1097
38:44.120 --> 38:46.000
I want it to be a surprise. Yeah.

1098
38:47.200 --> 38:48.730
Oh...

1099
38:49.390 --> 38:50.440
I get it now.

1100
38:51.650 --> 38:53.210
I'm jealous.

1101
38:53.480 --> 38:56.020
I wish I could have a family moment like this, too

1102
38:58.270 --> 39:00.600
Let me know if you need anything.

1103
39:00.980 --> 39:02.800
I will gladly help.

1104
39:03.940 --> 39:04.740
Anything at all?

1105
39:06.390 --> 39:06.960
Here.

1106
39:07.260 --> 39:08.360
I took everything out.

1107
39:08.590 --> 39:09.790
Now...

1108
39:10.680 --> 39:12.190
Put this on.

1109
39:12.640 --> 39:14.280
Mm...

1110
39:15.420 --> 39:16.240
Good...

1111
39:21.120 --> 39:23.870
[The D Dorm]

1112
39:25.120 --> 39:26.890
The salon was closed,

1113
39:27.610 --> 39:30.060
and the hot pot restaurant wouldn't let us inside.

1114
39:30.060 --> 39:32.410
This is all because of you two, Dollar and Dolly.

1115
39:32.590 --> 39:33.210
Hey...

1116
39:33.210 --> 39:35.400
Could it be because of your clothes that they didn't let us in?

1117
39:37.780 --> 39:38.400
- Hey. - Mom.

1118
39:38.400 --> 39:38.880
Hm?

1119
39:39.240 --> 39:40.400
Why didn't you lock the door?

1120
39:42.060 --> 39:42.720
I did.

1121
39:43.390 --> 39:44.260
You didn't.

1122
39:44.590 --> 39:45.100
Oh, no.

1123
39:45.600 --> 39:46.300
What do we do now?

1124
39:48.810 --> 39:49.680
Be careful...

1125
39:54.400 --> 39:56.200
- Whoa! - Ta-da!

1126
39:56.200 --> 39:57.640
This is a robbery.

1127
40:02.740 --> 40:04.380
Turn the lights on.

1128
40:04.380 --> 40:05.260
Ow...

1129
40:05.260 --> 40:06.560
- It's me. - Who is it?

1130
40:06.560 --> 40:07.820
Who?

1131
40:07.820 --> 40:08.840
It's Dew.

1132
40:08.970 --> 40:10.070
Dew?!

1133
40:10.440 --> 40:11.160
Yes, it's me.

1134
40:11.160 --> 40:11.600
What?

1135
40:12.190 --> 40:13.090
Wait.

1136
40:13.640 --> 40:15.370
- Everything is gone. - I'm sorry.

1137
40:15.370 --> 40:16.290
Don't tell me...

1138
40:16.590 --> 40:18.180
Did you rob my restaurant?

1139
40:18.460 --> 40:19.390
No,

1140
40:19.770 --> 40:21.790
I have a surprise for you.

1141
40:21.790 --> 40:22.280
Huh?

1142
40:23.160 --> 40:23.930
What surprise?

1143
40:26.050 --> 40:27.170
Let me go over it again.

1144
40:27.170 --> 40:27.790
Go on.

1145
40:28.040 --> 40:30.900
We'll surprise them by tricking them that I'm a thief.

1146
40:30.900 --> 40:31.390
Yeah.

1147
40:31.580 --> 40:33.050
- And you'll come in to help me. - Yes.

1148
40:33.050 --> 40:33.980
Like a superhero, right?

1149
40:33.980 --> 40:34.660
That's right.

1150
40:35.360 --> 40:37.860
Will this really impress them?

1151
40:37.860 --> 40:39.220
Of course it will.

1152
40:39.900 --> 40:40.810
Think of it like this,

1153
40:40.810 --> 40:43.890
I haven't seen my family in a long time,

1154
40:44.410 --> 40:45.420
and then suddenly

1155
40:45.740 --> 40:47.420
I show up to protect them.

1156
40:48.040 --> 40:48.970
Think about it.

1157
40:49.390 --> 40:53.610
They would be proud to have me as the head of the family,

1158
40:53.610 --> 40:54.190
right?

1159
40:54.690 --> 40:55.610
Oh.

1160
40:55.610 --> 40:56.280
Yeah.

1161
40:56.280 --> 40:57.200
I get it now.

1162
40:57.320 --> 40:58.060
Yeah.

1163
40:58.080 --> 40:59.280
Don't worry,

1164
40:59.940 --> 41:02.670
I’ll do my best as a thief.

1165
41:02.780 --> 41:04.120
That's great. Yeah.

1166
41:06.620 --> 41:07.610
Uncle,

1167
41:08.290 --> 41:09.320
where are you?

1168
41:09.610 --> 41:10.090
What?

1169
41:10.320 --> 41:10.780
Wait...

1170
41:10.990 --> 41:12.190
Who are you talking to?

1171
41:12.660 --> 41:13.900
Your husband.

1172
41:14.010 --> 41:14.880
- Huh?! - Huh?!

1173
41:15.370 --> 41:15.790
What?

1174
41:16.170 --> 41:17.520
Where is my dad, Dew?

1175
41:17.560 --> 41:18.190
Dad?

1176
41:19.440 --> 41:20.590
Uncle,

1177
41:20.860 --> 41:22.090
no need to hide anymore.

1178
41:23.130 --> 41:24.660
You can come out now, Uncle Wit.

1179
41:25.000 --> 41:25.720
Wait.

1180
41:26.120 --> 41:26.860
Uncle Wit?

1181
41:27.240 --> 41:28.120
- Mm. - Who is that?

1182
41:28.520 --> 41:30.190
My husband's name is Michael.

1183
41:30.530 --> 41:31.040
Huh?

1184
41:31.260 --> 41:32.000
Yes!

1185
41:35.860 --> 41:37.390
He isn't your husband?

1186
41:41.330 --> 41:42.010
He looks familiar.

1187
41:42.300 --> 41:42.900
Let me see.

1188
41:45.570 --> 41:46.140
No.

1189
41:46.140 --> 41:46.990
I know.

1190
41:47.960 --> 41:48.810
He’s the thief

1191
41:49.040 --> 41:50.590
that the police are after.

1192
41:50.770 --> 41:51.840
["WANTED" Royal Thai Police, Mr. Wit Tulrat, Age: 47 Years Old]

1193
41:51.860 --> 41:53.540
[Arrest Warrant: Residential Burglary]

1194
41:53.730 --> 41:55.110
- Hey... - Dew,

1195
41:55.800 --> 41:56.590
don't tell me...

1196
41:57.010 --> 41:58.850
you brought a thief here to rob my restaurant?

1197
41:58.850 --> 41:59.800
Oh, goodness.

1198
41:59.800 --> 42:00.520
I'm going to faint...

1199
42:00.520 --> 42:01.880
- Mom, Mom. - Mom.

1200
42:02.170 --> 42:03.450
It's okay, Mom.

1201
42:06.300 --> 42:07.390
It burns.

1202
42:07.390 --> 42:08.380
Please do not hurt me.

1203
42:08.590 --> 42:10.700
Please do not hurt me!

1204
42:10.700 --> 42:12.080
Take that!

1205
42:12.080 --> 42:13.760
Stop! It burns!

1206
42:13.760 --> 42:14.960
- Stop right there! - Are you challenging me?

1207
42:14.960 --> 42:16.480
- Stop! - Take my ritual knife.

1208
42:16.480 --> 42:17.540
- Here. - I am scared.

1209
42:17.570 --> 42:17.970
Stop.

1210
42:17.970 --> 42:18.960
Grandpa, I'm here to help you.

1211
42:21.610 --> 42:22.420
How dare you hurt Grandpa?

1212
42:23.180 --> 42:23.640
- Go. - Wait.

1213
42:23.980 --> 42:25.210
Hey, wait, wait.

1214
42:25.210 --> 42:25.810
Hey...

1215
42:25.860 --> 42:26.900
This is a misunderstanding.

1216
42:26.900 --> 42:27.790
Dobby, Dobby.

1217
42:28.600 --> 42:29.600
Dobby!

1218
42:30.050 --> 42:31.890
Dobby, stop!

1219
42:31.890 --> 42:32.460
How could I stop?

1220
42:32.460 --> 42:33.380
He hurt you this badly!

1221
42:33.380 --> 42:33.970
Yeah!

1222
42:35.180 --> 42:38.060
Tong used to be my neighbor!

1223
42:40.880 --> 42:41.570
He's your friend?

1224
42:41.570 --> 42:42.850
We used to be neighbors,

1225
42:42.850 --> 42:44.100
and we were very close.

1226
42:45.790 --> 42:46.280
Dobby...

1227
42:46.700 --> 42:47.260
Tong...

1228
42:47.420 --> 42:47.980
Dobby...

1229
42:48.330 --> 42:50.180
Why didn't you say anything earlier?

1230
42:50.180 --> 42:51.200
This way.

1231
42:52.820 --> 42:53.540
Ugh...

1232
42:54.110 --> 42:55.390
Your grandsons weren't

1233
42:55.600 --> 42:56.590
holding back, huh?

1234
42:57.410 --> 42:58.160
I'm sorry.

1235
43:00.560 --> 43:01.180
Dobby...

1236
43:01.570 --> 43:03.490
So the shaman is Gramps' friend?

1237
43:06.520 --> 43:07.260
No one shall save you!

1238
43:07.260 --> 43:10.420
The shaman is trying to seal me away.

1239
43:10.420 --> 43:13.020
I do not want to leave.

1240
43:13.020 --> 43:16.410
I have not met Gaysorn yet!

1241
43:17.860 --> 43:18.690
Gaysorn...?

1242
43:20.280 --> 43:21.240
Gaysorn...?

1243
43:22.210 --> 43:23.020
Gaysorn...

1244
43:26.210 --> 43:27.080
Danai?

1245
43:27.640 --> 43:28.990
It's really you.

1246
43:29.980 --> 43:30.900
Do you remember me?

1247
43:30.900 --> 43:31.780
I'm Tong.

1248
43:31.960 --> 43:33.460
The kid who lived next to your house.

1249
43:33.610 --> 43:34.450
Tong...

1250
43:35.440 --> 43:36.190
Tong,

1251
43:36.450 --> 43:37.390
son of Tor

1252
43:37.930 --> 43:38.730
and grandson of Toom,

1253
43:39.220 --> 43:40.360
who sold stoves in the market.

1254
43:40.520 --> 43:41.220
Tong,

1255
43:41.420 --> 43:43.200
who liked to fart in the tub.

1256
43:43.200 --> 43:45.140
After I got caught,

1257
43:45.140 --> 43:47.780
my father slapped me so hard I pooped everywhere.

1258
43:47.780 --> 43:49.390
Yeah, that's enough.

1259
43:49.390 --> 43:50.590
The more you say it...

1260
43:51.260 --> 43:51.900
the more disgusting it gets.

1261
43:52.720 --> 43:54.130
Come here.

1262
43:54.820 --> 43:56.260
Wait, wait.

1263
43:56.400 --> 43:58.990
What about Toi, Tor's brother and Ting's husband? Is he dead?

1264
43:59.130 --> 44:00.190
Tor and he died at the same time.

1265
44:00.190 --> 44:01.020
Tor...

1266
44:01.020 --> 44:02.100
Oh, don't do that!

1267
44:02.250 --> 44:03.410
Stop with all the alliterations.

1268
44:03.660 --> 44:04.410
I'm Tong.

1269
44:04.880 --> 44:06.000
Tong...

1270
44:06.560 --> 44:09.410
How did you end up as a shaman?

1271
44:09.650 --> 44:11.930
Well, after you broke up with Gaysorn

1272
44:12.050 --> 44:13.580
and were forced into a marriage,

1273
44:13.780 --> 44:15.410
you moved away.

1274
44:15.790 --> 44:17.590
I was forced

1275
44:17.620 --> 44:19.540
to study hard to become a medical student.

1276
44:19.540 --> 44:20.980
But I read from a wrong book.

1277
44:21.130 --> 44:22.380
I read from a book for spiritual intermediaries.

1278
44:22.650 --> 44:23.730
So I ended up becoming a spiritual healer,

1279
44:23.980 --> 44:25.390
- instead of a regular one. - Is that why you are a shaman?

1280
44:25.390 --> 44:26.000
Yes.

1281
44:26.290 --> 44:27.060
Oh...

1282
44:27.060 --> 44:27.790
What about you?

1283
44:28.090 --> 44:30.560
Why are you a spirit haunting this place?

1284
44:37.130 --> 44:38.440
If you guys really are friends,

1285
44:38.810 --> 44:40.420
why were you screaming in pain?

1286
44:40.780 --> 44:44.210
I wanted to know what it feels like

1287
44:44.420 --> 44:45.480
when sacred rice is thrown at you.

1288
44:45.480 --> 44:47.920
I saw it all the time in those TV dramas, you know?

1289
44:48.060 --> 44:49.150
I wanted to know what it feels like.

1290
44:49.170 --> 44:49.770
Mm,

1291
44:49.800 --> 44:50.920
it is pretty effective.

1292
44:50.920 --> 44:52.710
It burned all over.

1293
44:52.990 --> 44:53.820
Oh...

1294
44:54.330 --> 44:55.390
I was so worried.

1295
44:55.600 --> 44:57.120
I thought you were defeated.

1296
45:00.190 --> 45:01.760
You were worried about me?

1297
45:07.060 --> 45:08.320
I wasn't worried.

1298
45:08.590 --> 45:09.600
I was irritated, alright?

1299
45:10.580 --> 45:11.260
Yeah...

1300
45:11.580 --> 45:13.280
You disappeared for a few days,

1301
45:13.960 --> 45:15.060
and I didn't know where you went.

1302
45:18.190 --> 45:19.610
I did not go anywhere.

1303
45:19.740 --> 45:21.240
I was just wandering around.

1304
45:21.650 --> 45:22.990
I did not want to show up,

1305
45:23.130 --> 45:24.440
because I was sick of you.

1306
45:24.440 --> 45:26.050
I do not want to see your face.

1307
45:26.200 --> 45:28.210
Just go already. Go.

1308
45:28.420 --> 45:29.180
Go!

1309
45:31.390 --> 45:31.920
Dobby.

1310
45:31.920 --> 45:32.420
Dobby, where are you going?

1311
45:32.420 --> 45:32.980
We came all the way here to help.

1312
45:32.980 --> 45:34.690
Is Gramps friends with the shaman?

1313
45:35.900 --> 45:36.370
- Dobby. - He left.

1314
45:36.570 --> 45:37.290
Tell me.

1315
45:37.310 --> 45:39.710
- Dobby. - And they didn't even apologize.

1316
45:41.290 --> 45:42.540
It's a misunderstanding.

1317
45:42.540 --> 45:43.920
Danai, I don't understand.

1318
45:43.920 --> 45:45.790
Why didn't you just tell him

1319
45:45.920 --> 45:47.930
that you were gone because you went to

1320
45:47.930 --> 45:49.660
Nakhon Sawan to apologize to his mother?

1321
45:51.420 --> 45:52.180
I do not want all that trouble.

1322
45:52.820 --> 45:54.810
I do not want to argue with him.

1323
45:55.800 --> 45:57.040
Your grandson can hear you,

1324
45:57.790 --> 45:59.240
but you won't talk to him.

1325
46:00.020 --> 46:01.640
Your daughter can't hear you,

1326
46:01.840 --> 46:03.330
but you want to make it up to her, huh?

1327
46:03.600 --> 46:05.600
What do you want me to do?

1328
46:05.600 --> 46:06.190
Hm?

1329
46:06.420 --> 46:08.590
Confess to him?

1330
46:08.590 --> 46:09.580
Apologize to him and say,

1331
46:09.580 --> 46:10.990
"I am sorry

1332
46:11.220 --> 46:14.330
for trying to force your mother

1333
46:14.330 --> 46:17.410
to marry a degenerate like Surachet"?

1334
46:17.810 --> 46:20.760
If I did, he would spit in my face.

1335
46:21.180 --> 46:21.790
Danai,

1336
46:22.330 --> 46:25.010
is it that hard to admit you were wrong?

1337
